---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { published,articleUrl } from '../../lib/articles';
const entries=(await published()).filter(a=>a.data.lang==='en'&&(a.data.series==='ham-radio-sdr'||a.data.tags.some(t=>['ham-radio','sdr','packet-radio'].includes(t))));
---
<SiteLayout title="Ham Radio & SDR" alternateUrl="/no/series/ham-radio-sdr/"><p class="tag">SERIES / RADIO</p><h1>Ham Radio & SDR</h1><p>Amateur radio meets open technology: SDR receivers, Linux radio software, packet networking, digital modes, antennas, and reproducible lab experiments.</p><h2>Planned topics</h2><p>RTL-SDR on Linux, OpenWebRX, ADS-B (1090 MHz) and AIS reception (~162 MHz), APRS and Direwolf, AX.25 and packet-radio BBS, digital modes, and portable receiving stations.</p><p class="muted">Receiving and transmitting are different activities. Radio transmissions require appropriate authorization and compliance with local spectrum regulations. Technical experiments will be labelled as hardware-tested only after verification.</p><h2>Articles</h2>{entries.length ? <ul>{entries.map(a=><li><a href={articleUrl(a.id,'en')}>{a.data.title}</a></li>)}</ul> : <p class="muted">The first articles are in preparation.</p>}</SiteLayout>
